@segment   place-of-your-own
@title     The Place of Your Own
@levels    F27
@duration  ~2m30s
@protected Reception Centre

say From the gardens, allow yourself to be drawn toward the place that is yours.
pause 8
say You may already know where it is. Or not. Either is fine. Move in the direction that feels right, and you will arrive.
pause 12
say This is your place. What is here belongs to you.
pause 8
say The physical limitations you know do not apply here.
pause 6
say Here, intention shapes what is perceived. Set what you want, see how it can be, and it is so. The place morphs in front of you, as you wish.
pause 15
say You decide who comes here.
pause 6
say You may set a whitelist, naming those who are welcome. Or a blacklist, naming those who are not. You may invite specific individuals.
pause 12
say The systems are yours to design. The boundaries are yours to draw. This is your sovereign space.
pause 12
say And remember. When you wish company, when you wish to engage, when you wish to find activities or meet others, the Reception Centre is nearby. It is always nearby. You can return to it whenever you choose.
pause 10
